Electric Feel Publishing signed Swiss-German production duo The Elements , which is composed of Keven Wolfsohn and Paul Bogumil Goller. The duo executive produced Ayra Starr&#8217;s upcoming album Starr Girl . Other credits include contributions to tracks performed by Burna Boy (“It’s Plenty” and “Glory&#8221;), Pop Smoke (“Paranoia” featuring Gunna and Young Thug), Rema, Wizkid, Central Cee, Lewis Capaldi and Zara Larsson.

In a press release, the duo, which came out of the creative hub of Tape London, is described as having &#8220;a reputation for blending cutting-edge production with a deep understanding of global music culture, making them trusted collaborators for artists at the forefront of pop, hip-hop, and Afrobeat.&#8221;

“We&#8217;re grateful to&nbsp;the&nbsp;EF team for&nbsp;their support and vision, and we&#8217;re excited to build&nbsp;the&nbsp;next chapter of our sound together,&#8221; said The Elements in a statement. &#8220;Music has always been about pushing boundaries and creating records that connect with people around&nbsp;the&nbsp;world. Joining Electric Feel Entertainment gives us an incredible team to help take that vision even further.&#8221;

“We’re excited to welcome&nbsp;The&nbsp;Elements&nbsp;to Electric Feel Publishing,&#8221; added Austin Rosen , founder & CEO of Electric Feel Entertainment. &#8220;Bogo and Kev have built an incredible track record and have become trusted collaborators for some of&nbsp;the&nbsp;biggest artists in&nbsp;the&nbsp;world. We’re looking forward to working with&nbsp;them and supporting what’s next.&#8221;

Electric Feel&#8217;s roster also includes artists like Post Malone, as well as songwriters and producers such as Louis Bell, Billy Walsh, Nick Mira and Carter Lang. —&nbsp;Chris Eggertsen

